  "findings": [
    "Production crop proposals rise from 9 to 10, with the yellow/teal checker as the sole gain.",
    "The new checker proposal is visibly displaced. Against the existing approximate visible reference, its largest corner offset is 14.94% of mean square side length, well beyond the recorded reference uncertainty.",
    "The SAM baseline has 1.31% maximum corner offset on the same photograph; SAM with the diameter term removed has 2.67%. Accurate segmentation and a suitable crop objective are both needed.",
    "Known-region physical outline IoU of .975 did not certify correct overlap corners in this case.",
    "No full template replay is justified by this unconvincing new crop. Existing accepted production crops can also move; global objective removal is not adopted."
  ],
  "nextHypothesis": "Separate outer-cap colour purity from the reward for contrast across a lobe diameter. A valid shared/invisible cut or same-colour frame need not create a visible colour step. This is an untested mechanism, not yet a fix.",
